# MaintiQ — Industrial Failure Prediction with Explainable Artificial Intelligence

An academic machine-learning predictive-maintenance decision-support prototype.
MaintiQ predicts the binary `Machine failure` target using the AI4I 2020
Predictive Maintenance Dataset and explains model behaviour with SHAP and LIME.

## Status

This is an academic prototype under active development. See
`IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md` for phase progress and `docs/` for design documents.

## Purpose

Predict whether a machine will fail based on operational sensor readings, and
explain which features drove each prediction. It is a desktop decision-support
tool, not a certified industrial diagnostic product.

## Academic / safety notice

> **MaintiQ is an academic decision-support prototype using the AI4I 2020 benchmark
> dataset. Predictions and explanations are model outputs, not certified industrial
> diagnoses or maintenance instructions. Qualified human review is required.**

MaintiQ does not:
- diagnose real machinery,
- connect to, control, or send commands to machinery,
- claim live factory telemetry, PLC, SCADA, or MES integration,
- present SHAP/LIME contributions as causal explanations,
- present a model score as a guaranteed real-world failure probability unless
  calibration is implemented and verified.

## Technology stack

- Python 3.11+ (built and tested with Python 3.13 in this environment)
- PySide6 — native desktop GUI
- pandas / NumPy — tabular data
- scikit-learn — preprocessing, pipelines, models, metrics
- XGBoost — gradient boosting classifier
- SHAP / LIME — model explanations
- Matplotlib — charts and exported figures
- Joblib — model-pipeline serialization
- PyInstaller — Windows executable packaging
- Inno Setup — Windows installer (when available)

## Repository layout

```
